{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q411566","formula":"AlFePH₄O₇","hill":"AlFeH4O7P","elements":["H","O","Al","P","Fe"],"composition":{"H":4.0,"O":7.0,"P":1.0,"Al":1.0,"Fe":1.0},"names":{"en":"Childrenite","ru":"Чилдренит","uk":"Чилдреніт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Childrenite is a rare hydrated phosphate mineral with elements iron, manganese, aluminium, phosphorus, oxygen and hydrogen. Its chemical formula is (Fe2+,Mn)2+AlPO4(OH)2•H2O and it has a molecular weight of 229.83 g/mol. Its specific gravity is 3.2 and it has a Mohs hardness of 4.5 to 5.","ru":"Чилдренит — минерал из класса фосфатов. Назван в честь английского химика и минералого Джона Джорджа Чилдрена (1777—1852). Чилдренит является вторичным минералом, образующимся при изменении других фосфатов гранитных пегматитов.","uk":"Чилдреніт — мінерал, водний фосфат заліза та алюмінію. Названий на честь англійського мінералога Дж. Чілдрена (1823)."},"fame":13,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q411566","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Childrenite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A7%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%B4%D1%80%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%B8%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A7%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%B4%D1%80%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%96%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Childrenite-child-12c.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q5381929","formula":"MnAlPH₄O₇","names":{"en":"Eosphorite"},"elements":["H","O","Al","P","Mn"],"fame":